  "attestation": "D-133 closed-loop round 7 fixes on needs-wording (audit of d5d4b14: 1 HIGH, 4 MEDIUM, 2 LOW). HIGH-1 and MEDIUM-7, by a per-construct limit (the owner standing preference): a choice that acts (Apply, Change it differently, Keep it, Drop it, Confirm, Accept as mine, Keep/Revert, Change it) is offered only for a digest entry of ONE finding; an entry clustering several is answered in words (said, owed), and at apply a choice recorded on a multi-finding entry (an earlier hand-in offered it) is read as said; buildDigest clustering is unchanged. MEDIUM-2, MEDIUM-3, MEDIUM-4: Apply on knowledge-concern, spine-review-concern and detail-in-spine, Change it on fact-disputed, and interrupt and M5 answers are recorded exactly as before (ms8 acceptance and instructor-change-owed still read them) and also owed: the host-answer marker names the answer seq (owes), saidOwed lists such answers with their words until taken up, owedWords matches them; every recorded digest answer returns answer and words. LOW-5: a taken-up record without answers and binding reads binding from the answer marker kind (unknown kind: binding, fail-safe). LOW-6: when the act refuses after answerDigest logged the answer, a refused marker is written once, so later applies report already recorded. Probes adopted as tests/needs-wording.audit7.test.mjs (HIGH-1 and MEDIUM-7 follow the limit: a cluster offers no choice; a choice on a cluster from an earlier hand-in is read as words), registered for req.host.alembic-needs-wording and req.host.alembic-needs-apply. CHANGELOG Unreleased and alembic-job/CLAUDE.md updated; VERSION unchanged. Reviewed every required item. Tests, the full suite once (75 files: the 36 required plus alembic-needs, alembic-needs-wording, needs-wording audits 1-7, job-release, verdict-path, d49-decisions and all 27 red-team suites): 977 passed, 0 failed (COURSEWERK_FRAMES=installed, concurrency 2, one test process under the shared lock).",
